            <ArticleTitle>A universal genotyping-microarray constructed by ligating a universal fluorescence-probe with SNP-encoded flaps cleaved from multiplex invasive reactions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12922-12925</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06649j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To achieve a microarray universal to any SNP, we proposed a new way to construct a genotyping-microarray by ligating a universal fluorescence-probe with SNP-encoded flaps cleaved from invasive reactions on a slide surface. Our proposed microarray is labor-saving and cost-saving in setting up a new experiment for genotyping multiple SNPs, which is related to personalized medicine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
